          alt: "Table pairing common poisons with their antidotes — opioids and naloxone, paracetamol and acetylcysteine, organophosphates and atropine, benzodiazepines and flumazenil, warfarin and vitamin K, heparin and protamine, magnesium and calcium gluconate, iron and desferrioxamine, methaemoglobinaemia and methylene blue — the naloxone duration trap, and the rule that airway, breathing and circulation precede any antidote.",
          caption: "Airway, breathing and circulation come before any antidote. Naloxone lasts 30–90 minutes and the opioid lasts longer — the patient who wakes is watched until the opioid, not the naloxone, has worn off.",
